From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:57:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a compaction summary refused for its messages' shape
 is asked again as text (#3106)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A reply a network drop interrupted left an assistant message with
neither content nor tool_calls in the conversation. Ordinary turns
survive it — withoutSilentAssistants leaves the turn out of what a Chat
upstream is sent (#2599) — but Codex's compaction is the one request
that carries the whole conversation, so the one that still holds the
turn: a relay turned its summary request away for it, "AUBO: Invalid
assistant message: content or tool_calls must be set", on every model
of that upstream, while a laxer one answered the very same request. The
refusal was none of the asks-again-as-text cases, so codexCompact
handed the 400 back to Codex as it came, the compaction aborted, and
the turn reconnected.

refusesMessages is a 400 whose words are about the messages themselves
— the reported one, or the tool exchange a strict chat template refuses
— and it goes with the other conditions on the plain-text ask, which
has no assistant turns to refuse; when that fails too the summary is
magpie's own, as with the other refusals.

Fixes #3106

